---
description: Use a real JSON library, not hand-rolled string concatenation
alwaysApply: true
---

# JSON serialization

Do not build JSON by string concatenation or `StringBuilder` (e.g. manually
wrapping values in quotes and joining with commas). Hand-rolled string
escaping is easy to get subtly wrong — it is common to escape `"` but miss
`\`, control characters, or newlines — and the risk is highest for values
that did not originate from this application (an external service response,
user-supplied text), which is exactly the case most likely to contain a
character your escaping forgot.

Use the platform's JSON library instead:

- **Java**: `com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper` —
  `objectMapper.writeValueAsString(value)`. Inject/reuse one `ObjectMapper`
  rather than constructing one per call.
- **Groovy**: `groovy.json.JsonOutput.toJson(value)` or `new JsonBuilder(value)`
  for ad hoc serialization; `grails.converters.JSON` (`value as JSON`) where
  the codebase already renders through Grails' JSON converter.

This applies equally to a single scalar/array (e.g. a list of string codes
written into a JSON column) and to full request/response bodies — there is
no "too small to bother" case where hand-rolled string building is safer or
simpler than the library call.
